# kontra — the framework. Actors live in kontra-actors, workflows in kontra-workflows.

# THE OPERATOR'S OWN WORK, never the repo's: `kontra config` writes actors and
# caller workflows under .kontra/, and a checkout update must never touch them.
.kontra/

# python
.venv/
# A worktree usually SYMLINKS .venv to the main checkout's, and `.venv/` matches directories only.
.venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/

# generated: machine proto stubs (sdk/python/_gen, backend/_gen) are COMMITTED +
# CI drift-checked (buf generate + git diff --exit-code), so they are NOT ignored.
# Never edited by hand; their bytecode caches fall under the __pycache__ rule above.

# generated: per-actor build Dockerfiles (synthesized default / author + identity
# stamp) + the captured image digest (KONTRA_ACTOR_DIGEST, ADR 0011) written by
# scripts/build.sh

# The examples/ rules that lived here went with the directory (ADR 0038). Actors are in
# kontra-actors, workflows in kontra-workflows, and the offensive-security tooling that used to
# sit under examples/private/ — payload construction, probe corpora, detection heuristics — is
# not in any public repository: publishing it hands defenders a signature to filter on and hands
# everyone else a working scanner.

# run-actor output dirs (default --output) + scratch
out/
tmp/
tmp.jsonl
node_modules/

# demo scratch + compiled CLI binary
.demo/
cli/cli
cli/kontra
/kontra

# Compiled example-actor binaries. `go build ./...` inside a single-main-package module
# writes the executable into the module dir, so these reappear on every verification run.
# A 35 MB binary was tracked this way and re-committed by anyone who ran a build.
# Compiled example binaries — 52 MB each. These were listed one per example, so every
# NEW example leaked one until somebody noticed. Matched by shape instead: inside an
# example module, source and config all carry an extension and the binary never does.

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/

# Orchestrator runtime artifacts (SQLite run store + DuckLake dataset catalog) are
# ignored by backend/.gitignore — kept there so the patterns live in one place.

.scratch/
# kontra monitor --duckdb materialized files
kontra-*.duckdb

# Local runtime config — NEVER commit. .env carries live credentials (e.g. the DuckLake
# Postgres password, which belongs in a secret store, not the repo), and the compose
# override is per-machine wiring (host ports, network bridges) that must not bind others.
.env
docker-compose.override.yml

# generated from doctl at fleet-up time
ansible/inventory/hosts.ini
ansible/inventory/hosts.json
ansible/inventory/*.retry

# tofu state + provider plugins
infra/tofu/.terraform/
infra/tofu/*.tfstate*
infra/tofu/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Playwright's own output (ADR 0020's Dashboard specs). Traces are retained on failure only, and a
# retained trace is a debugging artifact, never a checked-in one.
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/blob-report/

# .kontra/ — this installation's own configuration and code, created by `kontra init`
# (install.sh runs it). Ignored WHOLE, and both halves matter:
#   config.yaml   live credentials — the DigitalOcean token, the Pulumi passphrase, four tokens
#   workflows/    an operator's own caller workflows
#   actors/       an operator's own actors
# The second half is not a security rule but an ownership one: what lives here is theirs, and a
# checkout update must never touch it. Examples belong in examples/.
.kontra/

# design-sync (docs/agents — /design-sync syncs this SPA to claude.ai/design).
# Committed: .design-sync/{config.json,NOTES.md,conventions.md,previews/,overrides/} — the sync's
# INPUTS, so a re-sync on any machine reproduces this build. Everything below is machine state:
#   .ds-sync/            the staged converter + its own node_modules
#   ds-bundle/           regenerated output, ~10 MB, uploaded not committed
#   .cache/ .learnings/  per-run verdicts and fan-out scratch
#   .ds-styles.css       Tailwind compiled for the previews (cfg.buildCmd emits it)
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules
frontend/.ds-styles.css

# Agent worktrees. `EnterWorktree` and `git worktree add` park checkouts here; each is a full
# working copy of this same repo, so committing one would nest the repo inside itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# Example-actor build output. `examples/` is source and is tracked; a built actor leaves a
# `__pycache__` beside its source, and the Go ones leave an extensionless binary named after
# their directory.

# Camoufox writes its persistent_context here when the `reddit` actor is served from the
# checkout (the actor sets user_data_dir="./camoufox_profile", so it lands in the CWD).
# 37 MB of browser profile, regenerated on every serve.
camoufox_profile/
